{"id": "EUVD-2026-86694", "enisaUuid": "c796ff74-9872-3c4d-a2ca-e43c6c2a5860", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Don't predict JMP32 pointer vs zero comparisons\n\nConsider the following program:\n\n        r1 = map_value;      /* low 32 bits are zero at runtime */\n        r6 = 0xdead000000000000;\n        if w1 != 0 goto l1;\n    l0: r1 += r6;\n        r2 = *(u64 *)(r1 + 0);\n        exit;\n    l1: r6 = 0;\n        goto l0;\n\nAt the moment is_branch_taken() reports the jump as always taken,\nbecause it does not distinguish between BPF_JMP and BPF_JMP32\ncomparisons when processing 'if w1 != 0 ...'.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:10", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e1544986536734166176c3add504add23bcbd15", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d16f0eafcaa62e677a2b5b0dabc1f8d31dfe3d4d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2ae33247e8b2dbe9d116d3e61cadf6d548339c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a4d7f94c1ca914469ced665ec2f98be669aef462", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e51179a4e09846f8fd0f26a05068520de2b301bf"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98041", "GHSA-2hhx-gj64-2962"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08baf087-63f8-3f8a-a99e-b31e69f9251c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cac616db39c207dc63465a4e05c6ce0e60b2cce4 <e51179a4e09846f8fd0f26a05068520de2b301bf"}, {"id": "1f947abb-15e2-3abf-8446-b3f9d74a4605", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cac616db39c207dc63465a4e05c6ce0e60b2cce4 <e2ae33247e8b2dbe9d116d3e61cadf6d548339c6"}, {"id": "2b225f87-83cd-3cf6-a2bd-0fd30b2c942f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "3c5e1799-57f0-3bcf-a77e-18c05c32ab13", "product": {"name": "L